              "Data in a GIS comes in two main forms. Vector data uses points (such as postboxes), lines (such as roads or rivers) and polygons (shapes with an area, such as fields or council wards). Raster data is a grid of cells, like the pixels of a satellite image or a map of rainfall, where each cell holds a value.",
